! Cabal-Place ~ RETIRED, the model walks on as Cabal-Realm

''This address stopped carrying the model.'' The whole substance — the hearth-beside framing, the verb-not-noun Mu, the Ostrom · Matrix/SSB · CRDT-tombstone braid, the BeeKEM epoch tie-break, Plane-B convergent-removal, the unswept corner, the seal, the two roots, the wax-stamp — walks on, unabridged, at:

<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>

''Why the name moved'' (operator ruling). Three words that once blurred now cut apart:
* ''Place'' — reserved for the identity-bearing Lararium: the hearth that holds a DID.
* ''vessel'' — the metal currently running the code (hardware/runtime), never the Place.
* ''realm'' — what a cabal actually names: ''an imagined place on the DreamNet, the superset of the members' shared infrastructure, represented as an imagined realm.'' It mints no DID and hosts on no single machine; it composes the members' own.

So ''cabal-place'' released the word ''place'' back to the hearth, and the model took the name that fits what it does.

''Anchors travel.'' `#the-seal` · `#the-unswept-corner` · `#two-roots` · `#the-wax-stamp` · `#governance` · `#the-tie-break` · `#verb-not-noun` all stand unchanged on `cabal-realm`; `#the-place` re-anchors as `#the-realm`. Follow any old fragment to the same section under the new root.

''The prior body lives in the graph's history'', never deleted — this residue keeps the old address answering, and answering forward.

<<~/ahu>>

